  "verseSrc": "Chapter 2, Verse 353",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the barricade and it is not the polling lead. It is the choice — by the government, whether the deficit is presented as arithmetic the public is trusted with before the vote rather than after it; by the students and unions, whether a demand is named that a budget could actually meet; by the centre and left, whether they answer the security question with a policy or merely with a denial that the question exists; and by the electorate, whether \"re-establish the rule of law\" is asked to specify which law, enforced by which courts, against whom. §2:353 does not distinguish between a strongman of the right and a strongman of the left; it identifies the offer itself — mastery — as the threat. Whether France's crisis produces a negotiated settlement or a president who promises to end the argument is not fixed by the deficit; it is a decision held by named ministers, named organisers and named voters, and one that a different choice could still make."
